{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>The first time</b><br>סמכוני. From the heavy [binyan] (the Hif'il)." "באשישות. Wine." "[רפדוני.] Let them place my cushioning [around me] — apples. And in the language of Kedar: סעדוני [support me], or חזקוני [strengthen me]." "<b>The second time</b><br>סמכוני באשישות — wine; רפדוני בתפוחים — let them spread apples whose fragrance I smell and which I eat together with the wine, like the practice of a sick person who has before him cakes of wine and apple." "<b>The third time</b><br>This is סמכוני באשישות, like the matter of לכו שברו בלא כסף ובלא מחיר יין וחלב (Isaiah 55:1)." "בתפוחים. Signs that you show me, and wonders, such that their report is throughout the whole land." "(שמאלו.) The morning and evening burnt offerings."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:00.603684609Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}